{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 170,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1905, Albert Einstein published a series\nof papers that many consider a starting point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4530,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the modern age of physics. But other than\n\"E equals m c squared\", most people only know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8700,
    "dDurationMs": 4791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Einstein was famous, not for what he\nwas famous. Since this week marks the 133rd"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13491,
    "dDurationMs": 3949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anniversary of his birth, as is customary\nin western traditions we will celebrate by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17440,
    "dDurationMs": 2589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "taking a brief tour of his scientific publications."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20029,
    "dDurationMs": 4851,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, his paper from March, 1905 on why light\nis a particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24880,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Einstein didn't just pull this idea out of\nthin air – he first noted that the light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28430,
    "dDurationMs": 4559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "emitted from something hot (like a lightbulb\nfilament), actually has the same energy distribution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32989,
    "dDurationMs": 3891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a gas, which is somewhat surprising if\nyou're a nineteenth century physicist who"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36880,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thinks that light is a continuous wave and\nvery much not a gas composed of individual"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41100,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "molecules. And while the idea that \"light\nbehaves kind of like a gas\" was already well"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44899,
    "dDurationMs": 4021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "known before Einstein, no one had taken the\nlogical but crazy next step to conclude that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48920,
    "dDurationMs": 4699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light must then be made of individual particles,\ntoo! So Einstein proposed that these \"light-quanta\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53619,
    "dDurationMs": 4091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were in fact real particles that could account\nfor a few recent and unexplained experiments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57710,
    "dDurationMs": 3759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "having to do with knocking electrons off of\nmetals or gas molecules. He turned out to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61469,
    "dDurationMs": 4101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be right on all counts and got a nobel prize\nfor his work… but that's a story for another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65570,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "day."
    } ]
  } ]
}
